  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Drought Response through Provision of Integrated Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Promotion (WASH) Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to save lives and avert displacement and disease outbreaks through access to clean water, sanitation, and hygiene promotion services. The project is targeting communities living in Banadir, Galkayo and Kismayo districts in Somalia. IOM is providing lifesaving water through temporary water trucking; rehabilitating/constructing water sources (boreholes) as an exit strategy to emergency water trucking; constructing sanitation facilities (household latrines); and distributing hygiene kits and conducting hygiene promotion messages/campaigns.</narrative>
  </description>
